X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Children's Author Visit - Eddie Hall
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260730T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260730T103000
UID:b22411b1b884019d54737c492625803d@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Storytime\, Summer Reading\, Children\n\nEddie Hall is a child
 ren's author and proud dad of three who lives in Central Pennsylvania with
  his wife and son. His newest book is titled Lighthouse. A quiet\, poetic 
 picture book about a lighthouse whose steady light endures through storms\
 , distance\, and time.At the edge of the sea\, a lighthouse stands watch. 
 Through storms\, calm nights\, shifting tides\, and passing seasons\, its 
 light continues to shine. With gentle illustrations and soft\, lyrical tex
 t\, Lighthouse invites readers to pause\, breathe\, and find their own mea
 ning in its warm glow.A calm\, reflective reading experience for children 
 and adults alike\, Lighthouse offers a quiet space for interpretation—wh
 ere meaning is not explained\, but discovered.A thoughtful book for reader
 s drawn to stillness\, symbolism\, and stories that linger beyond the fina
 l page.Books will be available for purchase.
LOCATION:Lititz\, LTZ Community Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/childrens-author-visit-e
 ddie-hall-183251
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
