SUMMARY:How Big Were the Dinosaurs by Lancaster County Parks
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260803T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260803T113000
UID:b72893b8392ef4a2beedfe0216593968@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Summer Reading\, Children\, Tweens\n\nSome dinosaurs\, such as
  the Barosaurus\, were quite large and may have weighed as much as 35 tons
 . But other dinosaurs\, such as Compsognathus\, were about the size of a c
 hicken and weighed only eight pounds. Join a Naturalist to learn just how 
 big they were in comparison to modern day creatures and landmarks by compl
 eting activities and putting your knowledge to the test! 🦕🦖*This pro
 gram is recommended for children ages 6 - 12. Registration for How Big Wer
 e the Dinosaurs  will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, July 22nd for Manheim 
 Township and East Lampeter residents and on Wednesday\, July 29th for resi
 dents of other municipalities.Accompanying Adults – This program is fo
 r adults and children to enjoy together. Please plan to attend and be enga
 ged with your child. Drop offs will not be permitted. Registration Require
 ments –  To help us manage our space\, please register every person who 
 will be attending\, including adults or siblings.  Cancellations- Please c
 heck your email prior to departing to verify that the program has not been
  cancelled. Library Program Policies   No Show – Patrons failing to ca
 ncel their registration for more than 2 library programs in a month will b
 e restricted from registering for future programs for a period of one mont
 h’s time. Please cancel your registrations at least 2 hours prior to the
  start of the program to allow those on the waiting list to be notified of
  their change in registration status. Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10
  minutes prior to the start of the program to allow for parking and ot
 her circumstances. The program will begin promptly at the designated time.
  At this time\, your spot will be forfeited to those on the wait list who 
 will be granted entry. If spots remain\, registrants may be allowed into t
 he program. However\, registrants will not be permitted to enter the p
 rogram 5 minutes past the start time. Photography - The Manheim Township P
 ublic Library Code of Conduct Policy prohibits photographing or video reco
 rding individuals (including children) without their consent (or in the ca
 se of a child\, the consent of a parent or guardian).
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center ABC
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/how-big-were-dinosaurs-l
 ancaster-county-parks-170778
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
