SUMMARY:West African Drum Presentation
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260803T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260803T183000
UID:55d6e96ae82e133e690d19be33e1fba7@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Music\, Presentation\, Teens\, Adults\n\nTammi Hessen\, a Lanc
 aster PA-based drummer who has been studying in the West African\, hand dr
 um tradition of djembe/dununs for 20 years\, gives a special presentation 
 at the library. Tammi believes that drumming can unite people from the ins
 ide-out and continues to celebrate the nature and power of the drum as a m
 usical instrument and tool for joy\, transformation\, and personal\, as 
 well as community\, healing. She teaches and performs in the local area\, 
 including as a Professor at Franklin & Marshall College. For teens and adu
 lts. Registration is requested.
LOCATION:Adamstown\, ADM Community Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/african-drum-circle-pres
 entation-168971
