 in us for an open\, beginner-friendly conversation designed for residents 
 who want to understand the technology behind the headlines. Professors Wil
 lie Wilson and Jacob Logas from the Responsible & Ethical AI Leadership (R
 EAL) Lab at Franklin & Marshall College will break down how the rise of AI
  has grown the demand for these facilities. No tech background required!We
 ’ll cover:The Basics: What data centers do\, how they work\, and why dem
 and for them is growing.The Impact: Practical pros\, cons\, energy and res
 ource usage\, and local community considerations.Ethics & Tech: The broade
 r societal and ethical questions surrounding digital infrastructure.Whethe
 r you're curious\, concerned\, or just looking to learn the basics\, bring
  your questions-- no question is too simple!
