DESCRIPTION:Arts & Crafts\, Summer Reading\, Teens\n\nCalling all creative
  teens! Come try your hand at paper quilling\, a unique art form where lon
 g strips of paper are rolled to create 3D art! All supplies will be provid
 ed!This program is for teens ages 13-18 years only. Registration will open
  at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, July 29th for Manheim Township and East Lampeter
  residents and on Wednesday\, August 5th for residents of other municipali
 ties.No Show – Patrons failing to cancel their registration for more tha
 n 2 library programs in a month will be restricted from registering for fu
 ture programs for a period of one month’s time. Please cancel your regis
 trations at least 2 hours prior to the start of the program to allow for t
 hose on the waiting list to be notified of their change in registration st
 atus.Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10 minutes prior to the start of the 
 program to allow for parking and other circumstances. The program will beg
 in promptly at the designated time. At this time\, your spot will be forfe
 ited to those on the wait list who will be granted entry. If spots remain\
 , registrants may be allowed into the program. However\, registrants will 
 not be permitted to enter the program 5 minutes past the start time.Check 
 In - All participants must provide an emergency contact number upon regist
 ration or at the start of the program.Drop Off Program – This program is
  intended for children over the age of 13 years who can participate indepe
 ndently. Adult(s) must be present to check in child with youth services st
 aff prior to program. Adults will not be allowed in the event space.
