BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/teen-book-talk-156960"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:CANCELLED : Teen Book Talk:  What the River Knows
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260824T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260824T190000
UID:ef593de17d6f65350f7257413d23dcb4@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Book Club\, Teens\n\nFor Teens ages 13-18 years of age only.Ca
 lling all teen readers! Join us for Teen Book Talk\, a fun and engaging mo
 nthly book discussion group led by members of our Teen Advisory Board! Boo
 k selections are chosen by teens during advisory meetings. Interested in j
 oining the Teen Advisory Board? Sign up through the library calendar. Each
  month\, we’ll dive into a new title—ranging from trending young adult
  fiction to graphic novels\, fantasy epics\, thought-provoking contemporar
 y stories\, and more.This month we'll be reading "What the River Knows" by
  Isabel Ibanez. Set in 1884\, nineteen-year-old Inez travels to Egypt afte
 r the sudden death of her parents to uncover the truth about their deaths\
 , and as she attempts to unravel the mysteries her parents sought\, she be
 comes a pawn in a larger game that threatens to kill her.  You’ll get th
 e chance to share your thoughts\, hear different perspectives\, and connec
 t with fellow book lovers in a relaxed and welcoming space. Snacks will be
  provided\, and occasionally we’ll have themed activities or giveaways t
 ied to the book!Note: To help everyone stay present and get the most out o
 f the experience\, we ask that all phones stay in pockets or bags during t
 he program. Thank you for your cooperation!Library Program PoliciesNo Show
  – Patrons failing to cancel their registration for more than 2 library 
 programs in a month will be restricted from registering for future program
 s for a period of one month’s time. Please cancel your registrations at 
 least 2 hours prior to the start of the program to allow for those on the 
 waiting list to be notified of their change in registration status.Late Ar
 rivals – Please arrive 10 minutes prior to the start of the program to a
 llow for parking and other circumstances. The program will begin promptly 
 at the designated time. At this time\, your spot will be forfeited to thos
 e on the wait list who will be granted entry. If spots remain\, registrant
 s may be allowed into the program. However\, registrants will not be permi
 tted to enter the program 5 minutes past the start time.Check In - All par
 ticipants must provide an emergency contact number upon registration or at
  the start of the program.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Study Room #119
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/teen-book-talk-156960
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/lego-block-party-172199"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Lego Block Party!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260824T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260824T190000
UID:ab1dae6301d6e6c03953e9d4a3404bf0@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:STEM\, Summer Reading\, Children\, Tweens\n\nRegistration for 
 Lego Block Party will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, August 12th for Manhei
 m Township and East Lampeter residents and on Wednesday\, August 19th for 
 residents of other municipalities.For youth ages 8-12 years of age only.Ch
 ildren ages 8 and older are welcome to attend the program independently. T
 he LEGO Block Party at the library is a fun and creative program where chi
 ldren ages 8-12 come together to build various creations using LEGO bricks
 . Participants often have the opportunity to work individually or in teams
  to design and construct imaginative structures\, vehicles\, and scenes ba
 sed on a theme or their own imagination. The club typically fosters collab
 oration\, problem-solving\, and fine motor skills while encouraging a love
  for building and creativity. It's a great way for community members to so
 cialize\, learn\, and have fun in a supportive environment.Library Program
  PoliciesNo Show – Patrons failing to cancel their registration for more
  than 2 library programs in a month will be restricted from registering fo
 r future programs for a period of one month’s time. Please cancel your r
 egistrations at least 2 hours prior to the start of the program to allow f
 or those on the waiting list to be notified of their change in registratio
 n status.Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10 minutes prior to the start of 
 the program to allow for parking and other circumstances. The program will
  begin promptly at the designated time. At this time\, your spot will be f
 orfeited to those on the wait list who will be granted entry. If spots rem
 ain\, registrants may be allowed into the program. However\, registrants w
 ill not be permitted to enter the program 5 minutes past the start time.Ch
 eck In - All participants must provide an emergency contact number upon re
 gistration or at the start of the program.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center A
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/lego-block-party-172199
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
