 ties tailored for preschool-aged kids. Each session focuses on building ea
 rly literacy\, motor skills\, and social interaction through playful explo
 ration.Perfect for ages 3–6 with an adult\, this program provides a welc
 oming and inclusive environment where kids can learn and grow together. Pa
 rents and caregivers are encouraged to participate and share in the joy of
  discovery with their little ones.Ms. Laura has over 20 years of preschool
  classroom experience bringing a wealth of knowledge in early childhood de
 velopment. Her approach focuses on creating a warm\, engaging\, and suppor
 tive environment where children can thrive.Adults attending with their chi
 ld(ren) do NOT need to register. Please add any additional registrants to 
 your registration if more than one child that will be participating in the
  program.Registration will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, August 26th for M
 anheim Township and East Lampeter residents and on Friday\, August 28th fo
 r residents of other municipalities.Storytime PoliciesNo Show – Patrons 
 failing to cancel their registration for more than 2 library programs in a
  month will be restricted from registering for future programs for a perio
 d of one month’s time. Please cancel your registrations at least 2 hours
  prior to the start of the program to allow for those on the waiting list 
 to be notified of their change in registration status.Late Arrivals – Pl
 ease arrive 10 minutes prior to the start of the program to allow for park
 ing and other circumstances. The program will begin promptly at the design
 ated time. At this time\, your spot will be forfeited to those on the wait
  list who will be granted entry. If spots remain\, registrants may be allo
 wed into the program. However\, registrants will not be permitted to enter
  the program 5 minutes past the start time.Accompanying Adults – This pr
 ogram is for adults and children to enjoy together. Please plan to attend 
