BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/reserved-adult-program-bats-171891"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:The Secret World of Pennsylvania’s Bats
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260909T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260909T194500
UID:00caf510e75dc6eb41c0ba42203a32ba@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Discussion\, Adults\, Seniors\n\nThink you know th
 e night? Think again. Behind the myths and "spooky" tropes lies one of the
  most efficient biological machines on the planet. Pennsylvania’s bats a
 re tactical hunters\, essential ecosystem anchors\, and currently\, they a
 re fighting an uphill battle for survival.Join the Lancaster County Depart
 ment of Parks & Recreation for an unfiltered look at the state of our skie
 s. We’re moving past the basics to explore the high-stakes world of our 
 six hibernating species and the seasonal migrators that cross our borders.
  We’ll discuss the grim reality of a 99% population collapse and the cas
 cading effect that has on our local environment—specifically when it com
 es to controlling the world’s most prolific killer: the mosquito.From th
 e bizarre evolutionary traits of bats across the globe to the specific con
 servation strategies needed right here in Lancaster County\, this program 
 is designed for those who want the real story. Come find out why these mas
 ters of the dark are the most important neighbors you’ve never met\, and
  how you can play a role in their recovery 🦇
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center B
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/reserved-adult-program-b
 ats-171891
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
