 preschool program designed to spark curiosity and a love for learning in y
 oung children! This program features stories\, songs\, and hands-on activi
 ties tailored for preschool-aged kids. Each session focuses on building ea
 rly literacy\, motor skills\, and social interaction through playful explo
 ration.Perfect for ages 3–6 with an adult\, this program provides a welc
 oming and inclusive environment where kids can learn and grow together. Pa
 rents and caregivers are encouraged to participate and share in the joy of
  discovery with their little ones.Ms. Laura has over 20 years of preschool
  classroom experience bringing a wealth of knowledge in early childhood de
 velopment. Her approach focuses on creating a warm\, engaging\, and suppor
 tive environment where children can thrive.Adults attending with their chi
 ld(ren) do NOT need to register. Please add any additional registrants to 
 your registration if more than one child that will be participating in the
  program.Registration will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, September 2nd for
  Manheim Township and East Lampeter residents and on Friday\, September 4t
 h for residents of other municipalities.Storytime PoliciesNo Show – Patr
 ons failing to cancel their registration for more than 2 library programs 
 in a month will be restricted from registering for future programs for a p
 eriod of one month’s time. Please cancel your registrations at least 2 h
 ours prior to the start of the program to allow for those on the waiting l
 ist to be notified of their change in registration status.Late Arrivals 
 – Please arrive 10 minutes prior to the start of the program to allow fo
 r parking and other circumstances. The program will begin promptly at the 
 designated time. At this time\, your spot will be forfeited to those on th
 e wait list who will be granted entry. If spots remain\, registrants may b
 e allowed into the program. However\, registrants will not be permitted to
  enter the program 5 minutes past the start time.Accompanying Adults – T
 his program is for adults and children to enjoy together. Please plan to a
 ttend and be engaged with your child. Drop offs will not be permitted.Canc
 ellations- Please check your email prior to departing to verify that the p
 rogram has not been cancelled.Program Limits - Patrons are limited to one 
 session of multiple session programs per week.Preschool Party Registration
  Requirements – All children who will be participating in the craft will
  need to be registered as a participant to allow for adequate supplies.
