BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/reserved-program-183104"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Decoding the Deck: Intro to Tarot History and Symbolism
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260923T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260923T200000
UID:3d3bbe19bf38d9c9fd2c6bf06f53b2cb@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Presentation\, Adults\, Seniors\n\nHave you ever been curious 
 about the history behind Tarot cards? Or maybe you bought a deck because t
 he artwork was gorgeous\, but now it’s just sitting on your shelf collec
 ting dust? ✨Join us for an engaging\, beginner-friendly workshop led by 
 local instructor Theresa from @claritymindretreat! Perfect for history buf
 fs and beginners alike\, this session dives into the rich cultural origins
  and evolution of the cards-- from their roots as a 15th-century Italian p
 arlor game to the modern day.What we'll cover:🌍 The Four Elements: How 
 the suits connect to Earth\, Air\, Fire\, and Water.🔢 Numerology Basics
 : Decoding the hidden meanings behind the numbers.👁️‍🗨️ Visual
  Language: How to read the symbols and storytelling hidden in the artwork.
 Whether you want to understand your own deck better or just love a good ar
 t history deep-dive\, this class is for you!✍️⚠️ Please note: This
  presentation is strictly educational and focused entirely on history\, ar
 t\, and symbolism. No live readings will be conducted!
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center B
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/reserved-program-183104
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
